&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor, maintain, and optimize IT infrastructure, including servers, networks, storage, and databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the full system lifecycle, including provisioning, installation, configuration, asset management, monitoring, maintenance, and decommissioning of various systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with vendors to procure and deploy new hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to issues and requests from the Operations and Technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in IT operations, systems engineering, or a related role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of networking protocols and tools (TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, VPN)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with scripting and automation tools (e.g., Bash, PowerShell, Python)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional capability debugging and solving complex issues related to both hardware, low level software, and networking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of network architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail in fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to respond to occasional off-hour emergencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
